1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,120
Hi, everyone. Firstly, I want to thank you for the support.

2
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:08,840
Difficult times like this are a great reminder how strong our industry is and we work together.

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:13,200
We are grateful to our partners that acted quickly to freeze the hacked assets,

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:17,800
to global law enforcement who are working with hand-in-hand to suggest this.

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:22,600
But most of all, we are grateful to our users for their patience and understanding.

6
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:25,800
We are also sure that we are working non-stop to resolve this,

7
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:29,200
to make the users hold and live up to your trust.

8
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:35,600
I want to be clear, we are committed to covering all hacked losses through our company funds.

9
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:38,000
Your assets are safe.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,800
The good news is that we are recovering stolen assets for users.

11
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:47,400
Binance has reserved over 6.34 billion of company funds to cover the stolen assets.

12
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:52,400
Five billion of these funds already help in exact token assets that are impacted

13
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:58,000
such as USDC, USDT, PTC, if PMB, etc.

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,800
I know many of you are still asking the same question.

15
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:05,400
How can Binance actually prove your assets are not affected?

16
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,000
Let me be direct about the first point.

17
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,200
We never use any customer funds, so they are not impacted.

18
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:16,600
What was affected in this incident was Binance owned hot wallet.

19
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:20,600
User assets are held under Binance established security architecture,

20
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,200
the vast majority sits in co-wallets,

21
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:27,400
and are only moved into a hot wallet when a user makes a withdrawal.

22
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:32,200
One more thing I want to share, Binance has always been built for the long-term.

23
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:36,800
Most of what we earn from day-to-day operations is held in crypto assets.

24
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:43,400
We have kept a lot of them in the company and reinvested them into the business and into security.

25
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:48,000
Because we believe in crypto and the long-term value of this industry.

26
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,400
This is precisely why we are able to absorb a lot of this size,

27
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:54,200
immediately with our own money.

28
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:57,400
We are working on the outstanding amount by buying the token assets

29
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:00,400
through market and OTC channels.

30
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,800
We will share more progress as soon as we can.

31
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:06,800
If you, as a user, are concerned,

32
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:10,000
we encourage you to check funds on your Binance account

33
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,400
with our initial proof of reserve for public verification,

34
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,000
which is targeting on Monday.

35
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:21,400
We can reach out to our customer service with any question.

36
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:26,000
Next, I want to give you an update on our understanding of the hack itself.

37
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:31,600
Our tech and security team are still deep in investigation of the hack.

38
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:33,800
This was not carried out by one person.

39
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:37,200
Our initial investigation suggested that the security incident

40
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:40,600
may have involved a compromised laptop.

41
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:46,200
However, our subsequent investigation has uncovered additional points of breach.

42
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,400
This was a complex attack.

43
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:51,600
The attacker also used self-destruct mechanism

44
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:54,200
that destroyed tooling and traces as they ran,

45
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:58,400
making it more difficult for us to trace and investigate.

46
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:02,800
The attacker used a known multi-senature protocol,

47
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,400
EIP 7702,

48
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:08,200
to obtain on-chain execution,

49
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:10,800
or prove over a hot wallet.

50
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:13,800
The delegation did not pass through our normal approval controls

51
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:16,000
and that's why we need to pause.

52
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,800
The withdrawal service to investigate, rebuild, and retest

53
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:23,800
the entire infrastructure system.

54
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:25,200
So what we're doing now?

55
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:28,600
First, we're rebuilding the withdrawal service.

56
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:34,200
And we're not switching it back until it passes rigorous testing.

57
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:40,400
We're very hopeful that users will be able to withdraw prior to the Sunday deadline,

58
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:43,200
which is on track to be written for the hours.

59
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:49,000
Secondly, we're conducting a full security review across the entire company

60
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,600
and points, cloud key management, signing everything.

61
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,600
Third, we're completing the purchase of the remaining assets

62
00:03:57,600 --> 00:04:01,600
and we'll verify in our proof of reserves.

63
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:05,000
We're sharing a full proof of reserves report by Monday

64
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:11,400
and we're hoping to get an initial view of the proof of reserves before that.

65
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:13,800
Fourth, we're working with law enforcement,

66
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:17,800
blockchain intelligence firm, token issuers, and other exchanges

67
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:20,400
to trace and recover stolen funds.

68
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:24,200
We'll do everything within our power to ensure that this bad actors

69
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:26,200
will be held accountable.

70
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:28,800
Lastly, this industry-wide effort,

71
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:33,000
and we are very grateful to our partners across the entire ecosystem,

72
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,200
will move very quickly to help and support.

73
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:38,000
We'll weather this storm.

74
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Thank you for the support and stay safe.
